# 00 · Project Context

## Purpose
Define a shared engineering baseline that works across:
- Flutter
- Android (Kotlin/Compose)
- iOS (SwiftUI)
- Next.js/TypeScript
- .NET
- APIs/microservices
- Enterprise applications

## Scope
This ruleset defines:
- Architecture and coding standards
- Quality, performance, testing, and security expectations
- API/data design rules
- UI/UX and accessibility expectations
- AI-assisted development guardrails
- Code review and build/release practices

## Working Principles
- Prefer reuse over reinvention.
- Keep solutions simple, explicit, and maintainable.
- Optimize for correctness and operability before optimization tricks.
- Favor incremental change over broad rewrites.

## Definition of Done (Baseline)
- The change is understandable by a new team member.
- Static checks/lints pass.
- Relevant automated tests pass.
- Security/privacy implications are addressed.
- Monitoring/logging is sufficient for troubleshooting.
- Release/rollback path is clear for production-impacting changes.

## Decision Framework
When choosing implementations:
1. Use existing project patterns first.
2. Use standard language/platform capabilities second.
3. Add dependencies only with clear value and maintenance confidence.
4. Introduce new abstractions only when repeated complexity proves the need.
